 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "stream is a list of chunks of printable ASCII text. In this part (inferred) the stop token may be split across several consecutive chunks, so only the concatenation shows it. Let k be the index of the chunk holding the first character of the first occurrence of \"<END>\" in the concatenation of all chunks. Return chunks 0..k-1 unchanged (empty chunks included) followed by the part of chunk k before the token when that part is non-empty. If the concatenation has no \"<END>\", return every chunk unchanged. Characters of the token that sit in later chunks are dropped with those chunks. Return a fresh list.",
  "provenance": [
   {
